            common_days = set(available_days) & set(operational_days)
            if common_days:
                scheduled_pairs.append((correspondent, unit))
    return scheduled_pairs
```

This function takes two lists as input: `correspondents` (a list of tuples containing correspondent names and their available days) and `units` (a list of tuples containing unit names and their operational days). It then iterates over each correspondent and unit, checking for common available and operational days using set intersection. If there are common days, it adds a tuple containing the correspondent name and unit name to the `scheduled_pairs` list. Finally, it returns the `scheduled_pairs` list.

